00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:45.700
So in the analytic
space, smart analytics,

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:52.030
critical to be using your
business data in an informed

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:54.300
and in a smart way.

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:57.160
There's a bunch of, certainly,
SAP operational data,

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:58.130
of course.

00:15:58.130 --> 00:16:00.730
But most of the data, right,
is in enterprise data stores.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:01.938
And they're disparate, right?

00:16:01.938 --> 00:16:04.542
Hard to make good use out
of disparate data stores.

00:16:04.542 --> 00:16:06.250
So this is where
BigQuery comes in, where

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:09.490
you can pull in your
HANA data, your SAP data,

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:11.470
you can pull in your
Enterprise data,

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:14.380
and then even in some cases,
external data sources,

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:18.880
